        },
        {
          "sourceDoi": "10.48550/arxiv.2002.02753",
          "targetDoi": "10.1007/s10851-019-00922-y",
          "snippet": "A prominent avenue to establish mathematical foundations of CNNs is through their analysis in terms of stability. This can be achieved by studying their invertibility properties (Behrmann et al, 2018;Chang et al, 2018), by exploiting sparse coding concepts (Romano et al, 2019), and by interpreting deep learning as a parameter identification or optimal control problem for ordinary differential equations (Haber &amp; Ruthotto, 2017;Thorpe &amp; van Gennip, 2018;Zhang &amp; Schaeffer, 2019). CNNs can also be connected to flows of diffeomorphisms (Rousseau et al, 2019) and to parabolic or hyperbolic PDEs (Li &amp; Shi, 2017;Arridge &amp; Hauptmann, 2019;Smets et al, 2020), where it is possible to transfer L 2 stability results (Ruthotto &amp; Haber, 2019).",
