          "snippet": "Deep residual networks or ResNets are widely used architectures that demonstrate state-of-the-art performance in complex statistical learning tasks with applications in various fields, such as computer vision [8,26], or speech recognition [41,42]. The popularity of ResNets originates from their remarkable performance in the ImageNet [37] and the MS COCO [33] image recognition competitions.",
